{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ice_energy_3d",
  "description": "The coupled 3-D ice-energy piece of stage 2 (deferred from ./ice_energy.esm): the full-field PISM enthalpy equation dE/dt = D(K D(E,z),z) - w dE/dz - (u dE/dx + v dE/dy) + sigma/rho over four 2x3-column sub-domains of the 31x31 test-F grid, integrated as a continuous PDE by the harness. The model is built on the validated single-column EnthalpyColumn (./ice_energy.esm): the same BOMBPROOF vertical diffusion/advection stencils and ColumnInterpolation maps (./energy_templates.esm), the same cold/temperate thermal-diffusivity switch, and the same basal melt rate, all lifted to the field (./energy_3d_templates.esm). The state E_f[i,j,lev_f] is the fine-grid enthalpy of the 2x3 block (C++ cells (i0..i0+1, j0..j0+2); the scalars i0/j0 hold the C++ indices of the block's west/south columns, per test; the block extent nb_i x nb_j = 2 x 3 matches the index sets i/j). All forcing and geometry are read from full-field 31x31 parameters (H_g, u_g, v_g, w_g, sig_g, E_cts_g, E_f_init_g) at the absolute esm indices (i0+i, j0+j); the per-column surface level is ks(i,j) = floor(H(i,j)/dz) capped at Mz_fine-1, spelled as a faq sum (esm has no floor op); the marginal flag follows EnergyModel::marginal (any of the 8 periodically wrapped neighbors thinner than 100 m, energy.margin_ice_thickness_limit); and the cold-temperate transition enthalpy is a baked full-field parameter E_cts_g computed with the C++ operation order, because the K switch at temperate bases is sensitive to the last bit (the column model bakes E_cts for the same reason). The horizontal advection is the new coupled piece: it reads the LIVE neighbor columns (index(E_f, i+/-1, j, k)) so the harness integrates the coupled PDE, with the block-edge ghosts frozen at the full-field initial enthalpy E_f_init_g. PISM evaluates its explicit horizontal-advection B-array at the OLD state, so the one-step reference trajectory and the live-coupling PDE differ by O(dt^2) in the horizontal exchange (~6e-5 J/kg over the 10-yr step, |u|/dx ~ 2e-13 s^-1; far below the assertion tolerances). Every test block is placed so the demo column's UPWIND neighbor is live in the block ((7,15): the test-F flow there is WESTWARD, so the upwind east neighbor (8,15) is in the block; (23,15) and (16,15): eastward flow, upwind west neighbor live; (15,13): southward flow, upwind north neighbor (15,14) live), and the block-edge ghosts it never reads carry ~zero velocity (v = 0 on the j = 15 meridian, u = 0 on the i = 15 meridian) or are marginal-gated. Ice-free columns (ks = 0) carry an identically zero RHS and stay at their initial column state -- the dump E_in of an ice-free column is the constant surface enthalpy Enth_ks, exactly as EnthalpyModel::update sets the whole column to Enth_ks; rows above the ice surface carry zero RHS and stay pinned to Enth_ks (baked into E_f_init_g / E_f_init on rows >= ks). The vertical forcing (u, v, w, sigma) is coarse-to-fine interpolated in-model from the storage-grid full-field parameters by energy_coarse_to_fine_field, and E_out is the storage-grid fine_to_coarse of the state, the quantity the dumps carry. Tests: four t = 0 algebraic chains (blocks w/e/dome/m) pinning the IC, the c2f machinery, the ks/marginal/H chains, the marginal gates, and the t = 0 horizontal advection against values computed from the dump; four one-10-yr-step tests (dt = 315569259.747 s) asserting E_out against the dump within the documented backward-Euler/ODE integration-scheme gap (per-level abs tolerances, measured by the single-column model for the same cells/cell classes and documented in the test descriptions; the dome column has u = v = 0 and is exactly the validated single-column trajectory, so the leaf's measured 35.1 J/kg temperate-base gap applies verbatim; the east-adjacent (16,15) is the only cell whose second fine layer starts at the cold-temperate transition at the last bit, switching the basal diffusivity entries to the temperate value ratio*K (ratio = 0.1) and enlarging the measured one-step bed gap to 391.98 J/kg with a 2.06e-11 m/s basal-melt-rate gap -- both measured with the single-column model, which the coupled bed result matches to 8e-6 J/kg; see the step_block_dome description), the pinned surface rows (machine-exact), the ice-free invariant, and the basal melt rate. The demonstration assertions (step_block_w and step_block_e, (7,15)/(23,15) lev 21) use a 0.1 J/kg tolerance that is tighter than the 1.32 J/kg horizontal-advection shift over the step, so a model WITHOUT the horizontal coupling fails them. Run the tests with --compiler interpreter (runtime-ifelse stencils, as in ice_energy.esm; the native compiler refuses the const-cadence K assembly). The full 31x31-field model with a 31x31 state is deferred: the dense-Jacobian/linear-solve cost of the harness's BDF integrator scales roughly as N^3 in the number of unknowns (~21 min per 10-yr step for 558 unknowns, ~2 min for 248), which made the 58k-unknown full field impractical (a previous attempt produced no output after 4+ hours); the four 2x3 blocks (~6 min per 10-yr step) cover the dome center, the west/east mid-radius and south azimuths, the marginal column, and the ice-free column, and are the coupled-field building blocks for stage 3. No C++ bugs found."
 },
 "solver": {
  "stiffness": "high",
  "reltol": 1e-08,
  "abstol": 0.01
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "i": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 2
  },
  "j": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 3
  },
  "gi": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 31
  },
  "gj": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 31
  },
  "nb": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 8
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "EnthalpyField3D": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./energy_templates.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "./ice_rheology_templates.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "./energy_3d_templates.esm"
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "E_f": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/kg",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid enthalpy of the nb_i x nb_j block (the PISM enthalpy solve state, the coupled 3-D field)."
    },
    "K": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2/s",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Effective thermal diffusivity k/(rho*c) (ratio*k/(rho*c) for temperate ice), assembled once from the INITIAL enthalpy exactly as enthSystemCtx::assemble_R; the basal entry K[i,j,1] switches on fine level 2 (the C++ R[0] special case)."
    },
    "w_eff": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid vertical velocity after the marginal gate (enthSystemCtx::init zeroes m_w for marginal columns when energy.margin_exclude_vertical_advection is set)."
    },
    "u_f": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid horizontal x-velocity (coarse_to_fine of the full-field storage-grid u_g at the block cells)."
    },
    "v_f": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid horizontal y-velocity (coarse_to_fine of v_g)."
    },
    "w_f": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid vertical velocity (coarse_to_fine of w_g)."
    },
    "sig_f": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid strain heating (coarse_to_fine of sig_g)."
    },
    "diffusion_term": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/(kg s)",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Vertical enthalpy diffusion D(K*D(E_f,z),z) with the BOMBPROOF column stencil, per block column."
    },
    "adv_term": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/(kg s)",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Vertical enthalpy advection stencil as it appears in the C++ tridiagonal (D = I - dt*M); its ODE contribution is the negative (physical -w*dE/dz)."
    },
    "hadv_term": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/(kg s)",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Explicit horizontal enthalpy advection with first-order upwinding, reading the LIVE neighbor columns (the coupled PDE) with the block-edge ghosts frozen at the full-field initial enthalpy."
    },
    "strain_term": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/(kg s)",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev_f"
     ],
     "description": "Strain heating sigma/rho on rows 1..ks (excluded at marginal columns when energy.margin_exclude_strain_heating is set)."
    },
    "E_out": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/kg",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Storage-grid output enthalpy (fine_to_coarse of E_f), the quantity the Stage-1 dumps carry."
    },
    "H": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Ice thickness of the block cells (from the full-field H_g)."
    },
    "ks_count": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Number of fine levels at or below the ice surface: sum over k of [z_f(k) <= H] (esm has no floor op; the C++ ks = min(floor(H/dz), Mz_fine-1) is this count minus 1)."
    },
    "ks": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Fine-grid top-of-ice level, 0-based (floor(H/dz) capped at Mz_fine-1, ColumnSystem::ks)."
    },
    "marginal": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Marginal-column flag (EnergyModel::marginal: 1 when any of the 8 periodically wrapped neighbors is thinner than 100 m)."
    },
    "p_base": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Ice pressure at the base (p_air = 0)."
    },
    "p_up": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Ice pressure one fine level above the base."
    },
    "Tpmp_base": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Pressure melting point at the base."
    },
    "Tpmp_up": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Pressure melting point one fine level above the base."
    },
    "cts_base": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/kg",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Cold-temperate transition enthalpy at the base (from the baked full-field E_cts_g)."
    },
    "cts_up": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/kg",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Cold-temperate transition enthalpy one fine level above the base."
    },
    "base_temperate": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "True when the base is temperate (E_f[i,j,1] >= cts_base), the till_water == 0 branch of EnthalpyModel::basal_melt_rate."
    },
    "k1_temperate": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "True when fine level 2 is temperate (the branch selecting the T-gradient heat flux in basal_melt_rate)."
    },
    "hf_up": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Upward conductive heat flux at the base: -k*(T_pmp gradient) if level 2 is temperate, else -K_0*(E[2]-E[1])/dz."
    },
    "bmelt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "description": "Basal melt rate (EnthalpyModel::basal_melt_rate): 0 for a cold base or an ice-free column, else (G_geo - hf_up)/(rho_ice*L(T_pmp)), floor 0."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 65.57377049180327,
     "description": "Fine-grid spacing (4000/61 m, ColumnInterpolation::init_fine_grid)."
    },
    "dx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 58064.516129,
     "description": "Horizontal grid spacing (Lx/31)."
    },
    "G": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/(kg m)",
     "default": -40.18,
     "description": "Basal enthalpy-flux gradient G = -q_geo/(rho_ice*dz^2*R[0]/dt) = -q_geo*c_ice/k_ice (set_basal_heat_flux), J/(kg m)."
    },
    "lambda": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "BOMBPROOF parameter (1 for cold columns; 0 if temperate ice present). The permissive initial state never exceeds the CTS outside the basal temperate cells, so the C++ compute_lambda() result 1.0 is baked (its w-dependent bound is >= 9.5 > 1 for the dumped w)."
    },
    "margin": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 100.0,
     "description": "energy.margin_ice_thickness_limit of the instrumented run."
    },
    "exclude_v_adv": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "energy.margin_exclude_vertical_advection (yes)."
    },
    "exclude_h_adv": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "energy.margin_exclude_horizontal_advection (yes)."
    },
    "exclude_strain_heat": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "energy.margin_exclude_strain_heating (yes)."
    },
    "rho_ice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "default": 910.0,
     "description": "Ice density."
    },
    "c_ice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/(kg K)",
     "default": 2009.0,
     "description": "Specific heat capacity of ice."
    },
    "k_ice": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/(m K)",
     "default": 2.1,
     "description": "Thermal conductivity of ice."
    },
    "ratio": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.1,
     "description": "energy.enthalpy.temperate_ice_thermal_conductivity_ratio."
    },
    "g": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "default": 9.81,
     "description": "Standard gravity."
    },
    "T_melting": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 273.15,
     "description": "Fresh-water melting point."
    },
    "T_0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 223.15,
     "description": "Reference temperature (enthalpy_converter.T_reference)."
    },
    "beta_Clausius_Clapeyron": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K/Pa",
     "default": 7.9e-08,
     "description": "Clausius-Clapeyron gradient."
    },
    "L_0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/kg",
     "default": 334000.0,
     "description": "Latent heat of fusion at 273.15 K."
    },
    "c_water": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "J/(kg K)",
     "default": 4170.0,
     "description": "Specific heat capacity of liquid water."
    },
    "OM1": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "energy.drainage_target_water_fraction."
    },
    "DR3": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1/s",
     "default": 1.58443823077064e-09,
     "description": "energy.drainage_maximum_rate (0.05/yr)."
    },
    "Ggeo": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 0.042,
     "description": "Basal geothermal flux (test-F G_geo), W/m^2."
    },
    "i0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "C++ x-index of the block's west column (the block covers C++ cells i0..i0+6; esm cell (i,j) of the block is C++ cell (i0+i-1, j0+j-1)). The block plus its 1-cell halo must fit in the 31x31 field: i0, j0 in 1..23."
    },
    "j0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "C++ y-index of the block's south column (see i0)."
    },
    "di_nb": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "nb"
     ],
     "default": [
      -1,
      -1,
      -1,
      0,
      0,
      1,
      1,
      1
     ],
     "description": "x-offsets of the 8 neighbors of the marginal-column check (EnergyModel::marginal)."
    },
    "dj_nb": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "nb"
     ],
     "default": [
      -1,
      0,
      1,
      -1,
      1,
      -1,
      0,
      1
     ],
     "description": "y-offsets of the 8 neighbors of the marginal-column check."
    },
