     "description": "Initial fine-grid enthalpy of the block (the slice of E_f_init_g at the block cells; tests override it with the slice of their block). The ic op rejects index/faq expressions, so the initial condition references this same-shaped parameter."
    },
    "nb_i": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 2.0,
     "description": "Block extent in the i direction (number of block columns), matching the size of the index set i; the horizontal-advection template's ghost fallback reads the frozen full-field initial enthalpy at (i0+nb_i+1, ...)."
    },
    "nb_j": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 3.0,
     "description": "Block extent in the j direction, matching the size of the index set j."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "_comment": "Initial condition: the block slice of the pinned dump E_in (surface row and atmosphere at Enth_ks per column).",
     "lhs": {
      "op": "ic",
      "args": [
       "E_f"
      ]
     },
     "rhs": "E_f_init"
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Block ice thickness from the full field (esm index i0+i is the 1-based index of C++ cell i0+i-1).",
     "lhs": "H",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "i"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "j"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "H_g",
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          "i0",
          "i"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          "j0",
          "j"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Number of fine levels at or below the ice surface (z_f(k) = (k-1)*dz <= H): the C++ ks = min(floor(H/dz), Mz_fine-1) is this count minus 1 (esm has no floor op).",
     "lhs": "ks_count",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "i"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "j"
       },
       "k": {
        "from": "lev_f"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "-",
             "args": [
              "k",
              1
             ]
            },
            "dz"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "H",
            "i",
            "j"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        1.0,
        0.0
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Fine-grid top-of-ice level, 0-based.",
     "lhs": "ks",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       "ks_count",
       1
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Marginal-column flag: any of the 8 periodically wrapped neighbors thinner than 100 m (EnergyModel::marginal; the cell itself is not checked).",
     "lhs": "marginal",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_marginal_column_field",
      "bindings": {
       "H": "H_g"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Fine-grid forcing: coarse_to_fine of the storage-grid full-field parameters at the block cells.",
     "lhs": "u_f",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_coarse_to_fine_field",
      "bindings": {
       "x": "u_g"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "v_f",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_coarse_to_fine_field",
      "bindings": {
       "x": "v_g"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "w_f",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_coarse_to_fine_field",
      "bindings": {
       "x": "w_g"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "sig_f",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_coarse_to_fine_field",
      "bindings": {
       "x": "sig_g"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Marginal-column vertical velocity gate (enthSystemCtx::init).",
     "lhs": "w_eff",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j",
       "k"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "i"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "j"
       },
       "k": {
        "from": "lev_f"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "and",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "marginal",
            "i",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          "exclude_v_adv"
         ]
        },
        0.0,
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "w_f",
          "i",
          "j",
          "k"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Thermal diffusivity assembled once from the INITIAL enthalpy (enthSystemCtx::assemble_R runs before the solve). The basal entry switches on fine level 2 (the C++ R[0] special case R[0] depends on Enth[1]); interior/upper entries switch on their own level. The CTS comes from the baked full-field E_cts_g (bit-exact with the C++ at temperate bases).",
     "lhs": "K",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j",
       "k"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "i"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "j"
       },
       "k": {
        "from": "lev_f"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "==",
         "args": [
          "k",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "energy_thermal_diffusivity",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "E_f_init",
            "i",
            "j",
            2
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "E_cts_g",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "i0",
              "i"
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j0",
              "j"
             ]
            },
            2
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "energy_thermal_diffusivity",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "E_f_init",
            "i",
            "j",
            "k"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "E_cts_g",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "i0",
              "i"
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j0",
              "j"
             ]
            },
            "k"
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Strain heating on rows 1..ks (sigma/rho per the C++ RHS), excluded at marginal columns.",
     "lhs": "strain_term",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j",
       "k"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "i"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "j"
       },
       "k": {
        "from": "lev_f"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "and",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "marginal",
            "i",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          "exclude_strain_heat"
         ]
        },
        0.0,
        {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "<=",
           "args": [
            "k",
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "ks",
              "i",
              "j"
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "/",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "sig_f",
              "i",
              "j",
              "k"
             ]
            },
            "rho_ice"
           ]
          },
          0.0
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Vertical enthalpy diffusion D(K*D(E_f,z),z), BOMBPROOF column stencil (energy_vertical_diffusion_field rewrites this compound at priority 10).",
     "lhs": "diffusion_term",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "K",
         {
          "op": "D",
          "args": [
           "E_f"
          ],
          "wrt": "z"
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "wrt": "z"
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Vertical enthalpy advection stencil as it appears in the C++ tridiagonal. The C++ system is D x = RHS with D = I - dt*M, so the advection's contribution to the ODE dE/dt = M E + b is the NEGATIVE of this stencil (physical -w*dE/dz).",
     "lhs": "adv_term",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_vertical_advection_field",
      "bindings": {
       "E": "E_f",
       "w": "w_eff"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "Explicit horizontal enthalpy advection with first-order upwinding, reading the LIVE neighbor columns (the coupled PDE; PISM's one-step B-array is frozen at the old state -- the difference is O(dt^2) ~ 6e-5 J/kg, see the metadata). Block-edge ghosts are frozen at the full-field initial enthalpy.",
     "lhs": "hadv_term",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "energy_horizontal_advection_field",
      "bindings": {
       "E": "E_f",
       "u": "u_f",
       "v": "v_f"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "The semi-discrete enthalpy equation: dE_f/dt = D(K D(E_f,z),z) - w dE_f/dz + horizontal advection + strain heating. Ice-free columns (ks = 0) carry an identically zero RHS (the C++ skips the solve and pins the column to Enth_ks, already baked into the initial condition); rows above the ice surface have zero RHS (all four terms vanish there), so the surface and atmosphere rows stay pinned at Enth_ks from the initial condition.",
